/-!
# Universal structural persistence of positional carry

This module assembles, without adding a global bridge axiom, the parts of the
carry geometry that are already certified for every material base `b ≥ 2`.

The word *invariant* has several typed meanings here:

* one carry step changes positional coordinates while preserving value;
* the carry pattern keeps certified operational ancestry through the explicit
  arithmetic tower;
* the quadratic relation `amplitude² = mass` selects the same exponent
  `1/2` in every nondegenerate base;
* the native real operator has the same radial domain in every camera, while
  its resonance predicate remains camera-indexed;
* the Green, bracket, trace, and return operators reconstruct the complete
  vertical state with the ratio `q = 1 / sqrt b`, which is exactly the
  critical carry amplitude at depth one;
* complex notation is an injective packaging of the two real coordinates and
  therefore cannot create or remove a finite camera zero;
* Green boundary defects and connected Richardson defects keep their exact,
  separately typed provenance.

The final certificate is universal over the base and camera parameters of
these concrete systems.  It does **not** say that every mathematical object is
generated by carry, that raw boundary closure supplies mass compatibility, or
that resonance times of arbitrary composite cameras are equal.
-/

open scoped ComplexConjugate InnerProduct

namespace CPFormal.Analytic.Cp

open CPFormal.Logic
